# The MAVLink Inspector, ported from Controls/MAVLinkInspector.cs, which SETUP's Advanced page's
# "MAVLink Inspector" button opens (GCSViews/ConfigurationView/ConfigAdvanced.cs:27-30).
#
# The claims: the window opens with Graph It disabled, "Show GCS Traffic" unticked, the history 50
# and nothing heard (MAVLinkInspector.cs:28-50, 176-272). At its 333 ms timer's ticks the tree
# lists "Vehicle 1", under it "Comp 1 MAV_COMP_ID_AUTOPILOT1", and under that each message the
# vehicle sends, its name, rate, id and bytes a second - "HEARTBEAT (1.0 Hz, " then the id and
# "21Bps" - and under a message its fields' names, values and .NET types (:57-174). The facts
# carry the id in their keys, as a `#` in a line here starts a comment. Selecting ATTITUDE's
# roll enables Graph It (:322-337); Graph It asks "Points of history?" and OK opens a graph of
# ATTITUDE.roll, its Y axis "[rad]", which fills as ATTITUDE comes, and disables Graph It
# (:341-446). Ticking "Show GCS Traffic" adds what this application sends - its heartbeat from
# 255/190 - as "Vehicle 255", "Comp 190 MAV_COMP_ID_MISSIONPLANNER" (:448-457). The close box
# ends it, and the Advanced page stays.
#
# Needs SITL copter on tcp:127.0.0.1:5760 started from tools/sitl/params/copter.parm, which streams
# ATTITUDE once asked. Run from the repository root as
#
#   tools/gui-test.sh tests/gui/config-mavlink-inspector.gui -- tcp:127.0.0.1:5760
#
# Not yet run: the budget is a guess, set by hand until a passing run records one.

screen setup
window 1600x1200
budget 15
# A config.xml of its own, so the "Points of history?" answer this script gives is not kept in
# the settings of the machine running it.
env MP_CONFIG_XML $WORK/config.xml

# The vehicle first, and its parameters, which are fetched as it is heard: the SETUP list is
# built again when they are in, and a click before that is a click the list may forget.
expect vehicle.count > 0
expect params.held > 1000
expect config.inspector.window false
click setup-page-ConfigAdvanced
expect setup.page ConfigAdvanced
expect config.advanced.buttons.enabled MAVLink Inspector,FFT

# The constructor: nothing heard yet, Graph It disabled.
click advanced-but_mavinspector
expect config.inspector.window true
expect config.inspector.opened 1
expect config.inspector.graphit false
expect config.inspector.gcstraffic false
expect config.inspector.history 50
expect config.inspector.prompt none
expect config.inspector.graphs 0

# The timer's ticks: the vehicle, its autopilot, and what it sends.
expect config.inspector.updates > 0
expect config.inspector.vehicles Vehicle 1
expect config.inspector.components.1 ~ Comp 1 MAV_COMP_ID_AUTOPILOT1
expect config.inspector.messages.1.1 > 5
expect config.inspector.message.1.1.0 ~ HEARTBEAT (
expect config.inspector.message.1.1.0 ~ Bps
expect config.inspector.message.1.1.30 ~ ATTITUDE (

# The tree opened down to ATTITUDE's fields, sorted by name: pitch first.
expect config.inspector.row.0 Vehicle 1
click inspector-toggle-1
expect config.inspector.row.1 ~ Comp 1 MAV_COMP_ID_AUTOPILOT1
click inspector-toggle-1-1
click inspector-toggle-1-1-30
expect config.inspector.type.1.1.30.roll System.Single
expect config.inspector.type.1.1.30.time_boot_ms System.UInt32
expect config.inspector.value.1.1.30.time_boot_ms > 0

# A field selected: Graph It enabled, the path kept.
click inspector-node-1-1-30-roll
expect config.inspector.graphit true
expect config.inspector.selected ~ ATTITUDE (
expect config.inspector.selected ~ roll

# Graph It: the question, OK with 50, and the graph of ATTITUDE.roll filling.
click inspector-graphit
expect config.inspector.prompt Points of history?
click inspector-points-ok
expect config.inspector.prompt none
expect config.inspector.graphs 1
expect config.inspector.graphit false
expect config.inspector.graph.0.curves ATTITUDE.roll
expect config.inspector.graph.0.yaxis [rad]
expect config.inspector.graph.0.points > 3
click inspector-graph-0-close
expect config.inspector.graphs 0

# Show GCS Traffic: this application's own packets, from 255/190.
click inspector-gcstraffic
expect config.inspector.gcstraffic true
expect config.inspector.vehicles Vehicle 1,Vehicle 255
expect config.inspector.components.255 Comp 190 MAV_COMP_ID_MISSIONPLANNER

# The close box; the page stays.
click inspector-close
expect config.inspector.window false
expect setup.page ConfigAdvanced
expect config.advanced.active true
